speechtext:
Mr. Chairman, with a view to extending the scope of the present legislation by including therein the caisses populaires and credit unions;
With a view to facilitating the granting of loans mentioned in this bill;

With a view to sparing inconvenience to prospective borrowers, especially those who live in communities where there are no chartered banks;
With a view to enabling thousands of Canadians who have deposited their savings in caisses populaires or credit unions to make those savings available to small businessmen; (Text):
I should like to move:
That clause 2 (a) be amended by adding after the word "applies" in line 6, the following:
"as well as co-operative lending institutions such as credit unions, caisses populaires, and others, recognized by the minister as qualified loan institutions."
